s:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/main-body_opening4.jpg?w=768 768w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/main-body_opening4.jpg?w=1024 1024w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/main-body_opening4.jpg?w=1536 1536w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/main-body_opening4.jpg?w=2048 2048w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/main-body_opening4.jpg?w=1900 1900w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/main-body_opening4.jpg?w=2850 2850w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 950px) 100vw, 950px\" \/><\/p>\n<p>Voil\u00e0:<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-large wp-image-5979143\" src=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/PXL_20260112_222230288.jpg?w=950&#038;resize=950%2C393\" alt=\"\" width=\"950\" height=\"393\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/PXL_20260112_222230288.jpg?w=4080 4080w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/PXL_20260112_222230288.jpg?w=300 300w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/PXL_20260112_222230288.jpg?w=768 768w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/PXL_20260112_222230288.jpg?w=1024 1024w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/PXL_20260112_222230288.jpg?w=1536 1536w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/PXL_20260112_222230288.jpg?w=2048 2048w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/PXL_20260112_222230288.jpg?w=1900 1900w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/PXL_20260112_222230288.jpg?w=2850 2850w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 950px) 100vw, 950px\" \/><\/p>\n<p>Boring half first:<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-large wp-image-5979125\" src=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_inside-7.jpg?w=950&#038;resize=950%2C715\" alt=\"\" width=\"950\" height=\"715\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_inside-7.jpg?w=4080 4080w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_inside-7.jpg?w=300 300w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_inside-7.jpg?w=768 768w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_inside-7.jpg?w=1024 1024w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_inside-7.jpg?w=1536 1536w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_inside-7.jpg?w=2048 2048w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_inside-7.jpg?w=1900 1900w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_inside-7.jpg?w=2850 2850w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 950px) 100vw, 950px\" \/><\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-large wp-image-5979126\" src=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_top.jpg?w=950&#038;resize=950%2C715\" alt=\"\" width=\"950\" height=\"715\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_top.jpg?w=4080 4080w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_top.jpg?w=300 300w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_top.jpg?w=768 768w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_top.jpg?w=1024 1024w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_top.jpg?w=1536 1536w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_top.jpg?w=2048 2048w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_top.jpg?w=1900 1900w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_top.jpg?w=2850 2850w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 950px) 100vw, 950px\" \/><\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-large wp-image-5979124\" src=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_bottom.jpg?w=950&#038;resize=950%2C715\" alt=\"\" width=\"950\" height=\"715\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_bottom.jpg?w=4080 4080w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_bottom.jpg?w=300 300w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_bottom.jpg?w=768 768w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_bottom.jpg?w=1024 1024w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_bottom.jpg?w=1536 1536w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_bottom.jpg?w=2048 2048w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_bottom.jpg?w=1900 1900w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/top-half_bottom.jpg?w=2850 2850w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 950px) 100vw, 950px\" \/><\/p>\n<h2>PCB constituent pieces<\/h2>\n<p>Now for the half we all <em>really<\/em> care about:<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_inside-7.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-large wp-image-5979086\" src=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_inside-7.jpg?w=950&#038;resize=950%2C715\" alt=\"\" width=\"950\" height=\"715\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_inside-7.jpg?w=4080 4080w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_inside-7.jpg?w=300 300w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_inside-7.jpg?w=768 768w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_inside-7.jpg?w=1024 1024w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_inside-7.jpg?w=1536 1536w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_inside-7.jpg?w=2048 2048w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_inside-7.jpg?w=1900 1900w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_inside-7.jpg?w=2850 2850w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 950px) 100vw, 950px\" \/><\/a><\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter wp-image-5979089 size-large\" src=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_top.jpg?w=950&#038;resize=950%2C715\" alt=\"\" width=\"950\" height=\"715\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_top.jpg?w=4080 4080w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_top.jpg?w=300 300w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_top.jpg?w=768 768w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_top.jpg?w=1024 1024w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_top.jpg?w=1536 1536w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_top.jpg?w=2048 2048w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_top.jpg?w=1900 1900w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_top.jpg?w=2850 2850w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 950px) 100vw, 950px\" \/><\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-large wp-image-5979085\" src=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_bottom.jpg?w=950&#038;resize=950%2C715\" alt=\"\" width=\"950\" height=\"715\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_bottom.jpg?w=4080 4080w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_bottom.jpg?w=300 300w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_bottom.jpg?w=768 768w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_bottom.jpg?w=1024 1024w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_bottom.jpg?w=1536 1536w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_bottom.jpg?w=2048 2048w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_bottom.jpg?w=1900 1900w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_bottom.jpg?w=2850 2850w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 950px) 100vw, 950px\" \/><\/p>\n<p>As with its Amazon smart plug predecessor, the analog and power portions are \u201c<a href=\"https:\/\/www.nytimes.com\/2023\/09\/08\/t-magazine\/vanilla-spice-blandness.html\">vanilla<\/a>\u201d:<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_left-side.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-large wp-image-5979087\" src=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_left-side.jpg?w=950&#038;resize=950%2C715\" alt=\"\" width=\"950\" height=\"715\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_left-side.jpg?w=4080 4080w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_left-side.jpg?w=300 300w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_left-side.jpg?w=768 768w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_left-side.jpg?w=1024 1024w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_left-side.jpg?w=1536 1536w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_left-side.jpg?w=2048 2048w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_left-side.jpg?w=1900 1900w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_left-side.jpg?w=2850 2850w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 950px) 100vw, 950px\" \/><\/a><\/p>\n<p>The off-white relay at far right on the main PCB, for example, is the <a href=\"https:\/\/www.hongfa.com\/product\/power-relay\/HF32FV-16\">HF32FV-16 from Hongfa<\/a>. Perhaps the most interesting aspect of the analog-and-power subsystem, at least to me, is the sizeable fuse below the pass-through ground connection, which I hadn\u2019t noticed in the Amazon-equivalent design (although perhaps I just overlooked it?). The digital mini-PCB abutting the relay, on the other hand, is where all the connectivity and control magic take place\u2026<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_right-side.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-large wp-image-5979088\" src=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_right-side.jpg?w=950&#038;resize=950%2C715\" alt=\"\" width=\"950\" height=\"715\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_right-side.jpg?w=4080 4080w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_right-side.jpg?w=300 300w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_right-side.jpg?w=768 768w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_right-side.jpg?w=1024 1024w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_right-side.jpg?w=1536 1536w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_right-side.jpg?w=2048 2048w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_right-side.jpg?w=1900 1900w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/bottom-half_right-side.jpg?w=2850 2850w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 950px) 100vw, 950px\" \/><\/a><\/p>\n<p>In the upper left corner is the multicolor LED whose glow (amber or\/or blue, and either steady or blinking, <a href=\"https:\/\/www.bhphotovideo.com\/lit_files\/656693.pdf\">depending on the operating mode of the moment<\/a>) shines through the aforementioned translucent gasket when the switch is powered up (and not switched off):<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-large wp-image-5979131\" src=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/network-connected.jpg?w=771&#038;resize=771%2C1024\" alt=\"\" width=\"771\" height=\"1024\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/network-connected.jpg?w=3072 3072w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/network-connected.jpg?w=226 226w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/network-connected.jpg?w=768 768w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/network-connected.jpg?w=771 771w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/network-connected.jpg?w=1157 1157w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/network-connected.jpg?w=1542 1542w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/network-connected.jpg?w=1900 1900w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/network-connected.jpg?w=2850 2850w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 771px) 100vw, 771px\" \/><\/p>\n<p>Those two unpopulated eight-lead IC sites below it are\u2026a titillating tease of what might be in a more advanced product variant? In the bottom left corner is the embedded 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi 1T1R antenna. And to its right is the \u201cbrains\u201d of the operation at the other end of the antenna connection, <a href=\"https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/RTL8710\">Realtek\u2019s RTL8710<\/a>, which supports a complete TCIP\/IP \u201cstack\u201d and integrates a <a href=\"https:\/\/hackaday.com\/2016\/07\/28\/new-chip-alert-rtl8710-a-cheaper-esp8266-competitor\/\">166 MHz Arm Cortex M3 processor core, 512 Kbytes of RAM and 1 Mbyte of flash memory<\/a>.<\/p>\n<h2>Stubborn solder<\/h2>\n<p>Speaking of power pass-throughs\u2026what about the <em>other<\/em> side of the main PCB? The obvious first step is to remove the screw whose head you might have already noticed in the earlier shot:<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-large wp-image-5979111\" src=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/screw.jpg?w=950&#038;resize=950%2C715\" alt=\"\" width=\"950\" height=\"715\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/screw.jpg?w=4080 4080w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/screw.jpg?w=300 300w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/screw.jpg?w=768 768w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/screw.jpg?w=1024 1024w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/screw.jpg?w=1536 1536w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/screw.jpg?w=2048 2048w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/screw.jpg?w=1900 1900w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/screw.jpg?w=2850 2850w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 950px) 100vw, 950px\" \/><\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-large wp-image-5979110\" src=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/screw_removed.jpg?w=950&#038;resize=950%2C715\" alt=\"\" width=\"950\" height=\"715\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/screw_removed.jpg?w=4080 4080w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/screw_removed.jpg?w=300 300w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/screw_removed.jpg?w=768 768w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/screw_removed.jpg?w=1024 1024w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/screw_removed.jpg?w=1536 1536w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/screw_removed.jpg?w=2048 2048w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/screw_removed.jpg?w=1900 1900w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/screw_removed.jpg?w=2850 2850w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 950px) 100vw, 950px\" \/><\/p>\n<p>But that wasn\u2019t enough to get the PCB to budge out of the chassis, at least meaningfully:<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/rear-plug_interconnect.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-large wp-image-5979109\" src=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/rear-plug_interconnect.jpg?w=950&#038;resize=950%2C715\" alt=\"\" width=\"950\" height=\"715\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/rear-plug_interconnect.jpg?w=4080 4080w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/rear-plug_interconnect.jpg?w=300 300w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/rear-plug_interconnect.jpg?w=768 768w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/rear-plug_interconnect.jpg?w=1024 1024w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/rear-plug_interconnect.jpg?w=1536 1536w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/rear-plug_interconnect.jpg?w=2048 2048w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/rear-plug_interconnect.jpg?w=1900 1900w, https:\/\/www.edn.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/rear-plug_interconnect.jpg?w=2850 2850w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 950px) 100vw, 950px\" \/><\/a><\/p>\n<p>Recall that in the Amazon smart plug design, not only the back panel\u2019s ground pin but also its neutral blade pass through intact to the front panel slots, albeit with the latter also split off at the source to power the PCB via a separate wire. The line blade is the only one that only goes directly to the PCB, where it\u2019s presumably switched prior to routing to the front panel load slot.<\/p>\n<p>In this design, that same switching scheme may very well be the case. But this time the back panel neutral connection <em>also<\/em> routes solely to the PCB. Note the two beefy solder points on the main PCB, one directly above the screw location and the other to the right of its solder sibling. I was unable to get either (far from both of) them either successfully unsoldered from above or snipped from below. And all I could discern on the underside of the PCB from peering through the gap were a few scattered additional passive components, anyway.<\/p>\n<p>So, sorry, folks, I threw in the towel and gave up. I\u2019m assuming that those two particular solder points, befitting the necessary stability not only electrically but also mechanically, i.e., physically, leveraged <a href=\"https:\/\/www.venture-mfg.com\/what-is-pcb-welding\/\">higher-temperature solid or silver solder<\/a> that my iron just wasn\u2019t up for. Or maybe I just wasn\u2019t sufficiently patient to wait long enough for the solder to melt (hey, it\u2019s happened before). Regardless, and as usual, I welcome your thoughts on what I <em>was<\/em> able to show you, or anything else related to this product and my teardown of it, for that matter, in the comments!<\/p>\n<p><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u2014<\/span><\/i><a href=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/author\/brian-dipert\/\"><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Brian Dipert<\/span><\/i><\/a><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> is the Principal at Sierra Media and a former technical editor at EDN Magazine, where he still regularly contributes as a freelancer.<\/span><\/i><\/p>\n<p><strong>Related Content<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/amazons-smart-plug-getting-inside-requires-more-than-just-a-tug\/\">Amazon\u2019s Smart Plug: Getting inside requires more than just a tug<\/a><\/li>\n<li><a href=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/how-smart-plugs-can-make-your-life-easier-and-safer\/\">How smart plugs can make your life easier and safer<\/a><\/li>\n<li><a href=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/smart-plug-provides-remote-control-functionality-for-home-devices-via-voice-command\/\">Smart plug provides remote control functionality for home devices via voice command<\/a><\/li>\n<li><a href=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/teardown-smart-plug-adds-energy-consumption-monitoring\/\">Teardown: Smart plug adds energy consumption monitoring<\/a><\/li>\n<li><a href=\"https:\/\/www.edn.com\/this-smart-plug-automatically-resets-your-router-when-your-internet-goes-out\/\">This smart plug automatically resets your router when your Internet goes out<\/a><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>With Amazon\u2019s smart plug teardown \u201cin the books\u201d, we turn our attention to some TP-Link counterparts, with hands-on testing results.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":434,"featured_media":5979116,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"_jetpack_newsletter_access":"","_jetpack_dont_email_post_to_subs":false,"_jetpack_newsletter_tier_id":0,"_jetpack_memberships_contains_paywalled_content":false,"_jetpack_memberships_contains_paid_content":false,"footnotes":"","jetpack_publicize_message":"TP-Link\u2019s Kasa HS103 teardown","jetpack_publicize_feature_enabled":true,"jetpack_social_post_already_shared":true,"jetp